; vecpush_charge_before_type_check: the allocation charge precedes the
; register read, so an exhausted budget decides the fault.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md orders the work within one instruction: pops, then the
; allocation charge, then validation. VECPUSH on a register holding an int
; is a TypeMismatch under a budget that admits the charge, and a
; MemoryLimitExceeded under one that does not -- the ordering is only
; observable at the boundary between the two.
;
; tests/vectors/README.md's fault-ordering table listed this row as pinned by
; xqvm_py's unit tests alone, because `Inputs` carried no memory budget and
; no vector could express it (QUI-1289). It now can: VECPUSH charges
; VEC_ELEMENT_BYTES (16 -- a Vec holds up to two elements' worth of buffer
; per live element), so the boundary is a budget of 15 against one of 16.
; This vector sits well below it at 0, so it stays about the ordering rather
; than about the exact charge.

PUSH 7
STOW r0          ; r0 holds an int, which VECPUSH would reject on type
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r0       ; charged before the register is read
HALT
